// Pipeline lex handoff fixture (MEMORY.md §3.2 row 17, INV-38).
// pipeLexUnit used to copy the lexer's lexErrors into a bare string[]
// parameter element by element (lexErrs.add(lx.lexErrors[i]) in a loop):
// the destination array + its growth intermediates were abandoned beside
// the lexer's original, and the growth rode the bare-array-through-helper
// shape (MEMORY.md §2 rule 5). The fix hands the lexer's array straight to
// the PipeLexOut holder by assignment (out.errs = lx.lexErrors, the same
// ownership-transfer shape as PipeParseOut.errors / INV-27), so the
// diagnostic collection is held exactly once per lex.
// This program depends on the handoff being byte-identical for valid
// sources (this fixture lexes clean: no diagnostics, tokens unaffected) and
// on the negative lex-diagnostic path staying byte-identical (see
// EXPECT.txt step 2): the holder carries the exact strings in the exact
// order the lexer appended them, and drvPrintDiagnostics walks them in
// order, so the grouped output and the exit(1) path are unchanged.
void main() {
    printline("pipeline-lex OK");
}
